WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.909
In medieval Cairo, a medicine could fail long after compounding.

00:00:04.909 --> 00:00:10.395
A syrup might sour, crystallize, or lose the consistency that made it usable.

00:00:10.395 --> 00:00:12.817
Reliability was a practical craft.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:21.175
Our clearest shop-facing witness is Minhaj al-dukkan, compiled in Cairo in twelve sixty.

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:27.795
The manuscript shown here is a later Egyptian copy from nineteen oh four, not the author's original.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.054
Sugar and rosewater were more than flavours.

00:00:33.054 --> 00:00:40.980
They formed vehicles whose concentration and handling helped determine how a medicine could be stored, dispensed, and recognized.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:52.689
A druggist dissolved ingredients, skimmed foam, strained suspended material, and watched the liquid thicken.

00:00:52.689 --> 00:00:59.417
The important endpoint was qiwam, a usable material consistency judged through skilled observation.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.930
No thermometer or modern microbial assay guided this work.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:14.300
Instead, repeated sensory observation and procedural judgement helped practitioners recognize burning, unwanted crystallization, or the signs of a changing preparation.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.163
Recipes also offered ways to correct material deviations.

00:01:19.163 --> 00:01:23.845
Yet the surviving manual documents procedures and professional ideals.

00:01:23.845 --> 00:01:27.925
It does not measure the outcome of every batch actually sold.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.662
When a drug was unavailable, substitution posed another challenge.

00:01:34.662 --> 00:01:38.713
Names, source, freshness, and functional resemblance mattered.

00:01:38.713 --> 00:01:43.417
An acknowledged replacement was different from undisclosed adulteration.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:53.468
Shop manuals, hospital formularies, Genizah documents, and market oversight texts show different parts of the story.

00:01:53.468 --> 00:01:59.277
They reveal efforts at dependability, not proof of clinical efficacy or modern GMP.
